{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Each man according to his eating.</b> That is, according to the measure of his household, whether many or few. And it says <b>his eating</b>, because the eating of all of them is counted as the eating of the man upon whom they depend — and the proof of this is what it says afterward, ״וַיָּמֹדּוּ בָעֹמֶר״ and so on, ״אִישׁ לְפִי אָכְלוֹ״ and so on, and it returned to say how much each one would take: ״עֹמֶר לַגֻּלְגֹּלֶת״, and it returned to say <b>the number</b> and so on — to say that they should make no distinction between small and great except according to the number of the persons, for all of them would be equal in eating the manna. And its saying <b>for those who are in his tent</b>, it intends to say that if a man or woman dwells in his tent whose provisions are not upon him yet they are in his vicinity — for them too the man shall gather. And the teaching of our Sages of blessed memory (Yoma 75a) will enlighten the eyes with the wonders of HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:48.389086029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}